class: runtime
profiles: standard
summary: a Linux program linked with --link=libc, where compiler.c_runtime is true, looks root and group zero up by ID and by name through the C library and NSS rather than reading /etc/passwd and /etc/group itself, finds the process's own account by name when it has one, and refuses an ID and a name no database holds, a name holding a colon and a buffer too small with ERANGE, and a name longer than any system's LOGIN_NAME_MAX with no_account, as runtime/posix-accounts does on a static one; the C library is given the caller's whole buffer, so group zero is found in the smallest buffer holding what the C library needs and the group's joined copy beside it
